                                                "sense_id": "e1a0c312-3f63-3461-ac5d-d47aef3064fe",
                                                "text": "Pack ice, at times mounting to a height of 35 ft., snow, fog, and floating mines all played their part in the disorganisation of railway services, and most of the train ferry services were completely suspended for a month or more; [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "399764f4-784d-495a-9bee-bd4f6fc6f159",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a0c312-3f63-3461-ac5d-d47aef3064fe",
                                                "text": "Even without the Channel tunnel, British Railways carry on a substantial exchange of traffic with the Continent by the various train ferries, which handle some 500,000 tons of cargo annually."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
